; error: 15:23: 'e' is given what fixed 'xs' owns, and nothing changes through what a fixed name owns; give it a copy: 'check(…).copy() at r'
; What 'fail' sends is given back as the failure, so a failure a fixed name
; owns can't be taken by a flex name either.

task check(xs: [int]@r) -> int ~ [int]@r
    <- fail xs
fi

task main()
    region r
    fixed xs = [1, 2, ...] at r
    match check(xs)
    case {n}
        show(n)
    case failure flex e
        e[0] = 9
    fi
fi
